==English==

===Etymology===
{{sense|New York City}} From {{bor|en|nl||[[nieuw|Nieuw]] [[Haarlem]]|new Haarlem}}, the original name of the area under the Dutch control, after {{m|nl|Haarlem}}, a city in the Netherlands.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}
# {{place|en|neighborhood|in northern|bor/Manhattan|co:Suf/New York|city:Suf/New York|s:Suf/New York|c/USA}}, currently known for its [[black]] [[population]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1952|author=[[w:Ralph Ellison|Ralph Ellison]]|title=[[w:Invisible Man|Invisible Man]] |publisher=Penguin Books (2014)|page=159|passage=This really was '''Harlem''', and now all the stories which I had heard of the city-within-a-city leaped alive in my mind.}}
# {{obsolete form of|en|Haarlem}}. {{place|en|city|r/Randstad|p/North Holland|c/Netherlands}}

===Noun===
# {{Of or related to Afro-American culture and society, especially 1920s to 1940s. E.g. The Harlem Renaissance cultural movement and ''The Billboard'' magazine's Harlem Hit Parade (1942-1945)}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1994|author=[[w:David Evans (Uni. of Memphis)|David Evans]]|title=[[w:Harlem Hamfats vol.1|Harlem Hamfats vol.1]] |publisher=Document Records CD DOCD-5271 (1994)|passage= '''Harlem''' had by 1936 become a code word for anything black, urban and sophisticated.}}
